<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project>

  <!--
    Trimming roots for a Blazor WebAssembly app that publishes trimmed.

    Trimming the BCL, the Components framework and Morph's own assemblies (verified reflection-free) is
    safe and worth a lot of payload. The conversion pipeline's reflection-heavy dependencies are not:
    DocumentFormat.OpenXml, AngleSharp, and ImageSharp (+ Drawing/Fonts) resolve types by name at
    runtime, so full-trim silently strips types they need and the failure surfaces only as a browser-side
    crash part-way through a conversion. Rooting each keeps it whole.

    Every assembly named here is guaranteed present: Morph.Blazor references Morph.ImageSharp and
    Morph.Pdf, which drag the rest. An unresolvable TrimmerRootAssembly is a hard ILLink error, so this
    list must not name anything optional.

    Residual risk: a rooted library reflecting into a *framework* type the trimmer removed. Validate a
    change here by running a real document through every output format on the published build.
  -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(PublishTrimmed)' == 'true'">
    <TrimmerRootAssembly Include="DocumentFormat.OpenXml" />
    <TrimmerRootAssembly Include="DocumentFormat.OpenXml.Framework" />
    <TrimmerRootAssembly Include="AngleSharp" />
    <TrimmerRootAssembly Include="SixLabors.ImageSharp" />
    <TrimmerRootAssembly Include="SixLabors.ImageSharp.Drawing" />
    <TrimmerRootAssembly Include="SixLabors.Fonts" />
    <TrimmerRootAssembly Include="SixLabors.PolygonClipper" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Two workarounds an AOT publish (RunAOTCompilation) needs, and nothing else does. Both lean on SDK
    surface that is internal (underscore-prefixed). If an SDK update stops honouring either, the AOT
    publish fails with a build error, never a runtime one: "Precompiling failed for ... aot-instances.dll"
    for the first, "Assertion at sgen-alloc.c:409, condition '*p == NULL' not met" for the second.

    1. PdfSharp stays interpreted. It is rooted whole above, and AOT compiles every method of an assembly
       rooted whole; PdfSharp.Snippets.Pdf.BouncyCastleSigner references BouncyCastle.Cryptography, which
       PdfSharp's package does not depend on, so that compile fails. The interpreter never loads the
       snippet. Only PDF export runs PdfSharp. Drop this once PdfSharp is rooted without its Snippets
       namespace, or depends on what its snippets use.

    2. SixLabors.Fonts' calling-convention attributes are trimmed away
       (Morph.Blazor.AotLinkAttributes.xml). Fonts 3.1+ declares its system-font P/Invokes with
       [UnmanagedCallConv(CallConvs = new[] { typeof(CallConvCdecl) })]; Mono's WebAssembly AOT compiler
       (10.0.13, and 11.0.0-rc.2 still) allocates a managed array while decoding that attribute and its GC
       asserts, before any method is compiled. A calling convention means nothing on browser-wasm. Drop
       this once https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/issues/136351 is fixed. The file is applied by the
       trimmer, so an AOT publish must also trim, which a Blazor WebAssembly publish does by default.
  -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(RunAOTCompilation)' == 'true'">
    <_AOT_InternalForceInterpretAssemblies Include="PdfSharp.dll" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(RunAOTCompilation)' == 'true'">
    <_ExtraTrimmerArgs>$(_ExtraTrimmerArgs) --link-attributes "$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)Morph.Blazor.AotLinkAttributes.xml"</_ExtraTrimmerArgs>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
